<%# locals: (compact: false) %>
<%# FUIME: how a submitted application becomes a venture that can sell.

    After apply, the product tells the founder to wait on Fuime. That wait is
    three human clicks (approve → activate → operator vetting) unless a cohort
    code already did them. Applications and Vetting were on the nav; Cohorts
    was not — so the path that auto-admits was the one nobody opened
    (TEEN_GROWTH G2).

    This card is the one-page runbook. It lives on the three queues, not in a
    markdown file, because the people who need it are already looking at one
    of those pages. Do not remove operator vetting from the solo path: under
    merchant-of-record it is the compensating control for Fuime being the
    legal seller (PLATFORM_REVIEW.md). A cohort records that decision in
    advance; it does not waive eligibility. %>

<div class="card mb2" id="admit-runbook">
  <h2 class="mt0 text-lg">How we admit</h2>

  <p class="mb1">
    A submitted application does not create a business. Work
    <strong>left to right</strong>:
  </p>

  <ol class="mt0 mb2 pl-4">
    <li>
      <strong>Approve</strong>: this venture should exist.
      <%= link_to "Applications", applications_admin_index_path %>, then
      Approve on the submission.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Activate</strong>: create the business. Same submission page.
      Read the blocker list first (usual causes: no guardian under Connect,
      or the free plan's one-venture wall).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Operator vetting</strong>: they may sell. This is revocable
      and asked again when something changes.
      <%= link_to "Operator vetting", operator_vetting_admin_index_path %>.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p class="mb1">
    <strong>Solo applicant</strong> =
    <%= link_to "Applications", applications_admin_index_path %>
    then
    <%= link_to "Operator vetting", operator_vetting_admin_index_path %>.
  </p>

  <p class="<%= compact ? "mb0" : "mb1" %>">
    <strong>Event / group</strong> =
    <%= link_to "a cohort code", cohorts_admin_index_path %>
    on the review step. Founders who enter it get approve, activate and
    vet automatically, attributed to you. Watch the roster
    <strong>Next step</strong> column left to right.
  </p>

  <% unless compact %>
    <p class="muted mb0 text-sm">
      A cohort does not waive the services-only scope or the operator age
      floor, and it never stands in for a parent. Do not turn vetting off
      until offer-level moderation exists.
    </p>
  <% end %>
</div>
